Fillets: a rounding riding on another's contact line (0016) taken the
other way round where its ride fails, its side on the line lying on the
face, and the corners at a rider's ends (mitcad#1499, after mitcad#1494).

Two roundings of a face F narrower than both, no ball touching the faces
beyond F on both sides: 0016 computes the earlier stripe A on its own faces
and lets the later one, B, roll on A's contact line on F (RideOnOverlap,
B's side on the line on a support face made from A's blend), the blends
meeting on that line (ApplyRides). On a plate 1.3 thick rounded with 1, or
on a roof slab's end face along a slope (1.3 wide), that failed:

- where B is longer than the line it rides on (the slope's edge riding on
  the underside's line), B's walk runs on past the line's ends and throws:
  the ride is now tried the other way round where it fails (A riding on
  B's line), the failed ride's entry removed;
- B's side on the line indexed the support, a face of no solid, so the
  corners at B's ends could not find their faces (ChFi3d_cherche_edge:
  "Failed to find edge", already with an end face's two rims and one
  vertical edge rounded): that side now lies on F, its curve's p-curve on
  F projected from its line, its transition (computed on the support)
  turned where F lies the other way in the solid; ApplyRides finds B's
  SurfData on F too, and B's points at the line's ends become A's also
  where a corner of several stripes made its own point there (within ten
  tolerances);
- a corner of three stripes with a rider (PerformThreeCorner) walked the
  pivot's ball and put the rider's ends off the line: such a corner is
  filled by PerformMoreThreeCorner, between the stripes cut where their
  contacts meet, and a plate of a corner with a rider is built with G0
  constraints (with G1 to the riders' surfaces one of two mirror-image
  corners of the plate came out folded);
- the clash check between stripes (ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter) skips two
  stripes that both end where a part ride's blends meet;
- a stripe the corners at both its ends cut down to nothing (one SurfData,
  its contacts points, its two end curves one curve: a plate's vertical
  edge between the sphere of the bottom corner and the riders' corner at
  the top, both cutting it at the height of the lines ridden on) left a
  face of no area: after ChFi3d_FilDS its surface and contacts leave the
  data structure and the corner at one end takes the other one's curve,
  with p-curves of its own along it (dropStripesCutToNothing).

